  "prefLabel": "Rev 601.10 Calibration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 601.10 “Calibration” means the process of ensuring the predictive accuracy of the CAMA model(s), through testing, which may include but not be limited to: determining the variable rates and adjustments from market analysis for land and land factors, costs and depreciation for a cost model, valuation rates and adjustments for a sales comparison model, and market rents and capitalization rates for an income model.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Rev 600) #10581, eff 5-1-14; ss by #13916, eff 3-28-24 (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Rev 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev600.html"
